{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794302007,"nonce":"4s8lHb5aybjo6Tb2kW9cIhQoVsI=","title":".structured() refuses a plan of several axis-aligned boxes","message":"shape.structured() only meshes a single rect/box. A layered stack or a box with a box-shaped hole (named regions joined by +, or |, -, \u0026) is refused as a CSG plan, so such cells can only be meshed by gmsh, whose free tets cluster badly around vertices and leave the largest errors there (seen on a periodic layered N1E cell against the Fresnel solution).\n\nWanted: a rectilinear lattice whose planes are the box faces, each slab spaced at the finest region size it crosses, regions by cell centroid, interface tags a|b and outer face names as on the gmsh path.","files":null}]}